# Brewfiles are lists without an order. When two Macs change them at the
# same time, both sides are almost always right — git should merge them
# instead of leaving behind a conflict for somebody to resolve by hand.
#
# The rule is meant for the data repository: install.sh puts this file
# there, and the test harness builds its world with it. Here in the
# program repository there are no Brewfiles, so it does nothing.
Brewfiles/* merge=union

# Groups too: a line each, and two Macs making groups at once must merge.
groups merge=union

# Encrypted, so there are no lines to merge. Let git call them binary
# and report a conflict honestly rather than glue two ciphertexts
# together -- that was measured, and it ruins the file silently.
Safe/** binary -merge
